1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:08,227
BioPilot Bench connects a protein file, a review request, and traceable results in one workspace.

2
00:00:09,473 --> 00:00:14,700
This demonstration uses the registered public Lipase A reference.

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:19,221
Upload the full-reference FASTA and describe the variant.

4
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:26,343
A request for S108A is refused by the local protection guard.

5
00:00:28,521 --> 00:00:34,700
No model request is sent, and the file is never silently replaced with another protein.

6
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:38,174
A32V passes local validation.

7
00:00:38,209 --> 00:00:45,163
The confirmation connects the uploaded file hash to position thirty-two and the pinned ESM checkpoint.

8
00:00:45,198 --> 00:00:49,460
Execution requires separate permission and cost acknowledgment.

9
00:00:49,494 --> 00:00:54,700
Call limits are enforced; actual provider billing remains unverified.

10
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:01,224
I now execute the approved review through Meta, MCP, and local ESM.

11
00:01:01,826 --> 00:01:07,678
Waiting is shortened in this edit; the execution and its recorded results are real.

12
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:14,700
The review completes with three Meta requests and nineteen scored candidates in this workspace.

13
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:22,091
The result contains nineteen alternatives at the approved position, ranked by one common code policy.

14
00:01:25,091 --> 00:01:29,594
Compare candidates without changing their saved scores or ranks.

15
00:01:32,594 --> 00:01:37,608
Select A32V and carry the same selection into Structure.

16
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:45,145
The public experimental reference checks where residues can actually be located.

17
00:01:48,145 --> 00:01:56,852
ESMFold2 provides a full wild-type structure, computed on an L40S GPU and saved for inspection.

18
00:01:59,852 --> 00:02:08,261
For A32V, a separate ESM3 run provides a full two-hundred-twelve-residue predicted structure.

19
00:02:11,261 --> 00:02:17,483
These optional structure views complement the same saved ESM-two candidate ranking.

20
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:26,054
Atlas adds an exact-reference database match, with its accession and source.

21
00:02:28,373 --> 00:02:33,700
This saved lookup supplies reference context without requesting a new fold.

22
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:39,273
Agent Trace shows the actual Meta validation and scoring requests.

23
00:02:40,024 --> 00:02:46,700
Meta coordinates permitted tools; code enforces constraints, computation, and ranking.

24
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:52,271
Evidence connects the uploaded file to the saved report and scoring record.

25
00:02:52,377 --> 00:02:59,700
BioPilot Bench brings sequence, structure, and traceable evidence into one review workspace.
